      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. WHAT IS A NOUN?"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Uncountable nouns take a singular verb and cannot be preceded by 'a/an' or converted into plural forms using '-s/-es'.",
        "Certain nouns like 'News', 'Mathematics', and 'Physics' appear plural in form but take singular verbs.",
        "Nouns such as 'Scissors', 'Spectacles', and 'Trousers' exist only in plural form and require plural verbs.",
        "The 'One of' construction requires a plural noun followed by a singular verb.",
        "'A number of' takes a plural verb, whereas 'The number of' takes a singular verb."
      ],
      "id": "49lrg97"
    },
